      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2014 International Society of Travel Medicine.",
        "AbstractText": "A woman stung by the box jellyfish Carybdea marsupialis (Cnidaria, Cubozoa) at a Spanish Mediterranean beach showed systemic manifestations over several months [pain far from the inoculation point, arthralgia, paresthesia, hyperesthesia, increase in eosinophils and immunoglobulin E (IgE)] in addition to the skin condition."
      },
